fn page_404() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\" style=\"text-align:center\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">404</p> <h1>Page not found</h1> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin:1rem auto\">The page you requested does not exist or has moved.</p> <div class=\"hero-actions\" style=\"justify-content:center\"> <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"/\">Go home</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/\">Documentation</a> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_about() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">About</p> <h1>A compiled language built around a native backend</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nRUDRA is a statically typed, compiled systems language. Its defining\n        traits are a native backend and a self-hosted compiler: <code>ruxc</code> is\n        written in RUDRA and turns a source file into a native Linux x86-64\n        executable directly.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.5rem\">Philosophy</h2> <p>\nRUDRA aims to be easy to read, predictable to compile, and honest about\n        its scope. The language favors a small, well-defined surface over a long\n        list of partially working features. Capabilities are added when they can\n        be compiled, run and verified.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Design goals</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Readable syntax.</strong> Familiar function, binding and control-flow forms.</li> <li><strong>Static type checking.</strong> Type errors are caught before a program runs.</li> <li><strong>Memory-safety orientation.</strong> Bounds checks, allocation guards and division-by-zero traps abort the program instead of corrupting memory.</li> <li><strong>A native backend.</strong> Source compiles to a static x86-64 Linux ELF executable with no runtime dependencies.</li> <li><strong>Honest scope.</strong> Documented capabilities match what the shipped toolchain does.</li> </ul> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">The ecosystem</h2> <p>\nAround the language sits a toolchain: the released compiler (<code>ruxc</code>) and a shell wrapper (<code>rudra</code>), plus\n        components in the source repository that are not yet released, such as a\n        language server, a formatter and a package tool. Each is presented independently on the\n<a href=\"/ecosystem\">Ecosystem</a> page with an accurate status so that\n        experimental and planned work is never presented as production ready.\n</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <h4>Self-hosted toolchain</h4> <p>\nRelease 1.1.0 is the self-hosted toolchain for Linux x86-64: a static\n          <code>ruxc</code> with zero runtime dependencies. The 1.0.x releases were the\n          earlier Rust-based toolchain and are not current. This site only\n          makes claims about the 1.1.0 release. See\n<a href=\"/transparency\">Transparency</a> for details.\n</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_account() -> str {
    return "<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"container narrow\"><h1>Account</h1><p>The RUDRA website has no user accounts and no sign-in. It stores no personal data and sets no cookies.</p><p>To report bugs, ask questions or follow releases, use the GitHub repository.</p><p><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/issues\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Issues</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Discussions</a></p></div></section>";
}
fn page_community() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Community</p> <h1>Join the RUDRA community</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nThe RUDRA community is hosted on GitHub Discussions. This gives every\n        participant a real account, moderation tools and notifications, with no\n        separate login to manage.\n</p> <div class=\"hero-actions\" style=\"margin:1.5rem 0\"> <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\">Open GitHub Discussions</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/issues\" rel=\"noopener\">Report a Bug</a> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Categories</h2> <p>Start or join a conversation in any category on GitHub Discussions:</p> <div class=\"grid grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"> <a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">General Discussion</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Open conversation about RUDRA.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Getting Help</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Questions and troubleshooting.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Language Development</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Syntax, semantics and language design.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Compiler and Runtime</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Compiler behavior, runtime and performance.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Ruxel Studio</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">The full-screen terminal IDE (source repository, not part of the 1.1.0 release).</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">AI and Autonomous Systems</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">AI-assisted and autonomous tooling.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Security Research</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Security discussion and responsible disclosure.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Tutorials and Learning</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Guides and learning resources.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Project Showcase</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Projects built with RUDRA.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Feature Requests</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Proposals for new capabilities.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Bug Reports</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Problem reports (also tracked in Issues).</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"display:block\"> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Announcements</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Official project announcements.</p> </a> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.5rem\">What the community platform provides</h2> <p>These capabilities are provided by GitHub Discussions:</p> <ul><li>Developer profiles and accounts.</li><li>Discussion threads with nested replies.</li><li>Search, tags and categories.</li><li>Markdown and code snippets.</li><li>Reactions and upvotes.</li><li>Accepted answers for questions.</li><li>Report and moderation tools.</li><li>Notifications and subscriptions.</li></ul> <div class=\"callout callout-warn\" style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\"> <h4>Not implemented on this website</h4> <p>To keep the platform secure and maintainable, the following are intentionally not built into this website:</p> <ul style=\"margin:0.5rem 0 0\"><li>Custom website login or registration.</li><li>A website-hosted user database or profiles.</li><li>A website-hosted notification system.</li><li>A custom developer dashboard with persistence.</li></ul> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_contact() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container narrow\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Support</p> <h1>Contact and support</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Choose the channel that fits your need. Public channels help the whole community.</p> <div class=\"grid grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Direct support</h3> <p>For account, licensing or private inquiries.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Questions and help</h3> <p>Ask the community and the maintainers.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Discussions</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Bug reports</h3> <p>Report defects and compatibility problems.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/issues\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Issues</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Security</h3> <p>Report a security concern responsibly.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/security\">Security policy</a> </div> </div> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <h4>When reporting an issue</h4> <p>Include your platform, the release you installed (for example 1.1.0), and a minimal example that reproduces the behavior.</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_developers() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Developer Hub</p> <h1>Build with RUDRA</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Everything you need to start building, reporting issues and following development.</p> <div class=\"grid grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:1.8rem\"> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Getting started</h3> <p>Install release 1.1.0 and compile your first program with <code>ruxc</code>.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/\">Start here</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>GitHub repository</h3> <p>Source distribution, releases and issue tracking.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra\" rel=\"noopener\">Open repository</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Report an issue</h3> <p>File bugs and compatibility reports on the issue tracker.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/issues\" rel=\"noopener\">Open issues</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Discuss and contribute</h3> <p>Feature requests, help and project showcases.</p> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/discussions\" rel=\"noopener\">Open discussions</a> </div> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.5rem\">Contributing</h2> <p>\nContributions, bug reports and feature requests are welcome through the\n        GitHub repository. Use Issues for defects and compatibility problems,\n        and Discussions for proposals and questions. When reporting a problem,\n        include your platform, the release version you installed (for example 1.1.0),\n        and a minimal example that reproduces the behavior.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Releases and versions</h2> <p>\nRelease history and downloadable assets with checksums are published on\n        the <a href=\"/downloads/\">Downloads</a> page and on the\n<a href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/releases\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub releases</a> page.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">License</h2> <p>\nThe RUDRA toolchain is free to use, including commercially. The authoritative license text is the <a href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/blob/master/LICENSE\" rel=\"noopener\">LICENSE file in the repository</a> and the LICENSE file included in each release.</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\"> <h4>Packages and libraries</h4> <p>\nA package directory is not published here. No third-party packages,\n          projects or integrations are listed unless they are real and verified.\n</p> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Contact</h2> <p>\nFor direct support and inquiries, email\n<a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>. For\n        public technical discussion, prefer GitHub Issues and Discussions so\n        answers help the whole community.\n</p> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_docs_compiler() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"docs-layout\"> <aside class=\"docs-side\" aria-label=\"Documentation navigation\"> <div> <h4>Introduction</h4> <a href=\"/docs/getting-started\" class=\"\">Getting Started</a><a href=\"/docs/installation\" class=\"\">Installation</a> </div><div> <h4>Language</h4> <a href=\"/docs/language-fundamentals\" class=\"\">Language Fundamentals</a><a href=\"/docs/variables-and-types\" class=\"\">Variables and Types</a><a href=\"/docs/functions\" class=\"\">Functions</a><a href=\"/docs/control-flow\" class=\"\">Control Flow</a><a href=\"/docs/structs-and-enums\" class=\"\">Structs and Enums</a><a href=\"/docs/modules\" class=\"\">Modules and Projects</a> </div><div> <h4>Reference</h4> <a href=\"/docs/standard-library\" class=\"\">Standard Library</a><a href=\"/docs/compiler\" class=\"active\">Compiler Guide</a><a href=\"/docs/examples\" class=\"\">Examples</a> </div><div> <h4>Help</h4> <a href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\" class=\"\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/docs/faq\" class=\"\">FAQ</a> </div> </aside> <article class=\"docs-main\"> <h1>Compiler Guide</h1>  <p class=\"lead\">The RUDRA 1.1.0 release ships two commands: <code>ruxc</code>, the self-hosted compiler, and <code>rudra</code>, a small shell wrapper around it.</p> <h2>ruxc</h2> <p><code>ruxc</code> is a static x86-64 Linux ELF written in RUDRA itself, with no runtime dependencies. Imports resolve only from the directory of the source file.</p> <table> <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td><code>ruxc file.rux output</code></td><td>Compile to a native executable named <code>output</code></td></tr> <tr><td><code>./output</code></td><td>Run it; the exit status is the return value of <code>main</code></td></tr> </tbody> </table> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"sh\"><code>ruxc hello.rux hello\n./hello</code></pre> </div>  <h2>rudra wrapper</h2> <p><code>rudra file.rux output</code> copies the standard library next to a temporary copy of your source and then compiles it. Use it when your program imports std modules.</p> <table> <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td><code>rudra file.rux output</code></td><td>Compile with the std library available for <code>import</code></td></tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The release does not include <code>rudrac</code>, <code>--run</code>, <code>-o</code>, <code>--version</code>, or the subcommands <code>rudra new</code>, <code>run</code>, <code>build</code>, <code>check</code>, <code>clean</code>, <code>doctor</code> and <code>version</code>. A new RUDRA-written driver (<code>rudra build/run/check/version</code>) exists in the source repository but is not yet released.</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\"> <h4>Type checking</h4> <p>The compiler reports type errors and refuses to produce a binary. For example, <code>let x: int = \"a\";</code> fails with <code>TYPE mismatch</code> and exit status 1.</p> </div>  <nav class=\"docs-nav-fb\" aria-label=\"Pagination\"> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/standard-library\">Previous: Standard Library</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/examples\">Next: Examples</a> </nav> </article> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_docs_control_flow() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"docs-layout\"> <aside class=\"docs-side\" aria-label=\"Documentation navigation\"> <div> <h4>Introduction</h4> <a href=\"/docs/getting-started\" class=\"\">Getting Started</a><a href=\"/docs/installation\" class=\"\">Installation</a> </div><div> <h4>Language</h4> <a href=\"/docs/language-fundamentals\" class=\"\">Language Fundamentals</a><a href=\"/docs/variables-and-types\" class=\"\">Variables and Types</a><a href=\"/docs/functions\" class=\"\">Functions</a><a href=\"/docs/control-flow\" class=\"active\">Control Flow</a><a href=\"/docs/structs-and-enums\" class=\"\">Structs and Enums</a><a href=\"/docs/modules\" class=\"\">Modules and Projects</a> </div><div> <h4>Reference</h4> <a href=\"/docs/standard-library\" class=\"\">Standard Library</a><a href=\"/docs/compiler\" class=\"\">Compiler Guide</a><a href=\"/docs/examples\" class=\"\">Examples</a> </div><div> <h4>Help</h4> <a href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\" class=\"\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/docs/faq\" class=\"\">FAQ</a> </div> </aside> <article class=\"docs-main\"> <h1>Control Flow</h1>  <p class=\"lead\">RUDRA provides conditional branching and loops with a familiar shape. The samples below are complete programs: <code>print</code> takes only a string and adds no newline, and the exit status is the value <code>main</code> returns.</p> <h2>Conditionals</h2> <p>This program prints <code>medium</code>.</p> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>fn classify(n: int) -&gt; str {\n    if n &gt; 10 {\n        return &quot;big&quot;;\n    } else if n &gt; 5 {\n        return &quot;medium&quot;;\n    } else {\n        return &quot;small&quot;;\n    }\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(classify(7) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <h2>While loops</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>fn main() -&gt; int {\n    let mut i = 0;\n    let mut total = 0;\n    while i &lt; 5 {\n        total = total + i;\n        i = i + 1;\n    }\n    print(to_str(total) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>This program prints <code>10</code>.</p> <h2>For loops over a range</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>fn main() -&gt; int {\n    for k in 0..3 {\n        print(to_str(k) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    }\n    let xs = list_new();\n    push(xs, 4);\n    push(xs, 8);\n    for v in xs {\n        if v == 4 {\n            continue;\n        }\n        print(to_str(v) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>The range <code>0..3</code> yields <code>0</code>, <code>1</code> and <code>2</code>. <code>for v in list</code> iterates a <code>list[int]</code>; <code>break</code> and <code>continue</code> work in all loops. The program above prints <code>0</code>, <code>1</code>, <code>2</code> and <code>8</code>, one per line.</p> <h2>Operators</h2> <p>Arithmetic: <code>+ - * / %</code>. Comparison: <code>== != &lt; &gt; &lt;= &gt;=</code>. Logical: <code>&amp;&amp; || !</code>.</p>  <nav class=\"docs-nav-fb\" aria-label=\"Pagination\"> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/functions\">Previous: Functions</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/structs-and-enums\">Next: Structs and Enums</a> </nav> </article> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_docs_examples() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"docs-layout\"> <aside class=\"docs-side\" aria-label=\"Documentation navigation\"> <div> <h4>Introduction</h4> <a href=\"/docs/getting-started\" class=\"\">Getting Started</a><a href=\"/docs/installation\" class=\"\">Installation</a> </div><div> <h4>Language</h4> <a href=\"/docs/language-fundamentals\" class=\"\">Language Fundamentals</a><a href=\"/docs/variables-and-types\" class=\"\">Variables and Types</a><a href=\"/docs/functions\" class=\"\">Functions</a><a href=\"/docs/control-flow\" class=\"\">Control Flow</a><a href=\"/docs/structs-and-enums\" class=\"\">Structs and Enums</a><a href=\"/docs/modules\" class=\"\">Modules and Projects</a> </div><div> <h4>Reference</h4> <a href=\"/docs/standard-library\" class=\"\">Standard Library</a><a href=\"/docs/compiler\" class=\"\">Compiler Guide</a><a href=\"/docs/examples\" class=\"active\">Examples</a> </div><div> <h4>Help</h4> <a href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\" class=\"\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/docs/faq\" class=\"\">FAQ</a> </div> </aside> <article class=\"docs-main\"> <h1>Examples</h1>  <p class=\"lead\">Each example below is a complete program that was compiled with the released <code>ruxc</code> and run. Compile with <code>ruxc file.rux out &amp;&amp; ./out</code>.</p> <h2>Sum of a range</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>fn main() -&gt; int {\n    let mut i = 0;\n    let mut total = 0;\n    while i &lt; 5 {\n        total = total + i;\n        i = i + 1;\n    }\n    print(to_str(total) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>Prints <code>10</code>.</p> <h2>Factorial</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>fn factorial(n: int) -&gt; int {\n    if n &lt;= 1 {\n        return 1;\n    }\n    return n * factorial(n - 1);\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(to_str(factorial(5)) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>Prints <code>120</code>.</p> <h2>Struct and function</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>struct Point { x: int, y: int }\nfn manhattan(p: Point) -&gt; int {\n    return p.x + p.y;\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    let p = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n    print(to_str(manhattan(p)) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>Prints <code>7</code>.</p> <h2>Enum classification</h2> <div class=\"codeblock-wrap\" style=\"position:relative\">  <pre class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"rux\"><code>enum Sign { Neg, Zero, Pos }\nfn sign(n: int) -&gt; Sign {\n    if n &lt; 0 { return Sign.Neg; }\n    if n &gt; 0 { return Sign.Pos; }\n    return Sign.Zero;\n}\nfn label(s: Sign) -&gt; str {\n    match s {\n        Sign.Neg =&gt; { return &quot;negative&quot;; }\n        Sign.Zero =&gt; { return &quot;zero&quot;; }\n        Sign.Pos =&gt; { return &quot;positive&quot;; }\n    }\n    return &quot;&quot;;\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(label(sign(0 - 9)) + &quot;\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</code></pre> </div> <p>Prints <code>negative</code>.</p>  <nav class=\"docs-nav-fb\" aria-label=\"Pagination\"> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/compiler\">Previous: Compiler Guide</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\">Next: Troubleshooting</a> </nav> </article> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_docs_faq() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"docs-layout\"> <aside class=\"docs-side\" aria-label=\"Documentation navigation\"> <div> <h4>Introduction</h4> <a href=\"/docs/getting-started\" class=\"\">Getting Started</a><a href=\"/docs/installation\" class=\"\">Installation</a> </div><div> <h4>Language</h4> <a href=\"/docs/language-fundamentals\" class=\"\">Language Fundamentals</a><a href=\"/docs/variables-and-types\" class=\"\">Variables and Types</a><a href=\"/docs/functions\" class=\"\">Functions</a><a href=\"/docs/control-flow\" class=\"\">Control Flow</a><a href=\"/docs/structs-and-enums\" class=\"\">Structs and Enums</a><a href=\"/docs/modules\" class=\"\">Modules and Projects</a> </div><div> <h4>Reference</h4> <a href=\"/docs/standard-library\" class=\"\">Standard Library</a><a href=\"/docs/compiler\" class=\"\">Compiler Guide</a><a href=\"/docs/examples\" class=\"\">Examples</a> </div><div> <h4>Help</h4> <a href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\" class=\"\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/docs/faq\" class=\"active\">FAQ</a> </div> </aside> <article class=\"docs-main\"> <h1>FAQ</h1>  <p class=\"lead\">Honest answers to common questions.</p> <h2>What is RUDRA?</h2> <p>A compiled, statically typed systems language. Its compiler, <code>ruxc</code>, is written in RUDRA itself and turns a source file into a native x86-64 Linux executable.</p> <h2>Which platforms are supported?</h2> <p>The current 1.1.0 release targets Linux x86-64 only, as a tarball and a <code>.deb</code>. The 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 releases were the earlier Rust-based toolchain, which had macOS and Windows installers; those are not the current toolchain. See <a href=\"/downloads/\">Downloads</a>.</p> <h2>Are the distributed binaries dependency-free?</h2> <p>Yes. <code>ruxc</code> is a static ELF with no runtime dependencies, and the executables it produces are static ELF files too. They are not dynamically linked.</p> <h2>Does RUDRA support threads, channels and HTTP?</h2> <p>Not as language built-ins. There are no <code>spawn</code>, mutex, channel, <code>http_get</code> or <code>json_get</code> builtins. The standard library contains modules such as <code>thread</code>, <code>net</code>, <code>http</code> and <code>json</code>, but they have documented limits and should not be treated as production networking. TLS cryptography is implemented in RUDRA, but it is not wired into a live authenticated HTTPS client. See <a href=\"/transparency\">Transparency</a> for exact statuses.</p> <h2>Is there a package registry?</h2> <p>No. The 1.1.0 release does not include <code>ruxpkg</code>. A manifest-verifying package tool exists in the source repository but is not yet released, and no public package directory is published on this site.</p> <h2>What is the license?</h2> <p>The RUDRA toolchain is free to use, including commercially, and the programs you build are yours. The authoritative license text is the <a href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra/blob/master/LICENSE\" rel=\"noopener\">LICENSE file in the repository</a> and the LICENSE file included in each release.</p> <h2>How do I report a bug or request a feature?</h2> <p>Use the GitHub Issues tracker for bugs and GitHub Discussions for proposals. See <a href=\"/developers\">Developer Hub</a> and <a href=\"/community\">Community</a>.</p>  <nav class=\"docs-nav-fb\" aria-label=\"Pagination\"> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\">Previous: Troubleshooting</a> <span></span> </nav> </article> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
